### To Reproduce

Right now the drizzle adapter has this config set
```ts
 supportsJSON:
        config.provider === "pg" // even though mysql also supports it, mysql requires to pass stringified json anyway.
          ? true
          : false,
      supportsArrays: config.provider === "pg" ? true : false,
```
this makes it so when json is being handed to drizzle the adapter does a json stringify itself,
I am using sqlite with D1, which supports JSON and array
now the generated schema says `redirectUris: text("redirect_uris", { mode: "json" }).notNull()` but you hand drizzle a JSON string and it does its own stringify before storing it, effiectively doing a double stringify. Now because the behaviour is consistent better-auth itself works properly, but I get issues when doing quires with normal drizzle

```ts
 const clients = await db.query.oauthClient.findMany({
      where: and(eq(oauthClient.disabled, false), isNull(oauthClient.userId)),
      orderBy: desc(oauthClient.createdAt),
    });

console.log(clients);
```
this logs
```ts
{
    id: 'ABWDJdLG0ZCsGqGEwAt1tkyi7Si0g6VG',
    clientId: 'mNdDtvLrnpKexqjOxmCjwqfqVRLQLZcq',
    clientSecret: 'REDACTED',
    disabled: false,
    skipConsent: null,
    enableEndSession: null,
    subjectType: null,
    scopes: null,
    userId: null,
    name: 'Iterate',
    uri: null,
    icon: null,
    contacts: null,
    tos: null,
    policy: null,
    softwareId: null,
    softwareVersion: null,
    softwareStatement: null,
    redirectUris: '["https://localhost"]',
    postLogoutRedirectUris: null,
    tokenEndpointAuthMethod: 'client_secret_basic',
    grantTypes: '["authorization_code"]',
    responseTypes: '["code"]',
    public: false,
    type: null,
    requirePKCE: null,
    referenceId: null,
    metadata: null,
    createdAt: 2026-03-17T16:01:40.000Z,
    updatedAt: 2026-03-17T16:01:40.000Z
  }
```
this is a problem because now I have to hunt through the stringified json fields and parse it myself, even tho they are typed as `text("", {mode:"json"})`, they are not auto parsed because they were double JSON stringified

now there are solutions for this,
- put sqlite as a provider that supports JOSN and array (some versions of sqlite might not??)
- allow me to pass values for `supports*` (best for back compat)

### Current vs. Expected behavior

in my sqlite db stored value should look like a normal JSON stringify: `["https://localhost"]`
but in reality its a double JSON stringify, `"[\"https://localhost\"]"`

this causes issues when querying the db with drizzle directly

